1
00:00:01,296 --> 00:00:30,155
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sama Sambuddhasa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sama Sambuddhasa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sama Sambuddhasa Homage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble Buddha.

2
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:39,918
and fully self-awakened one.

3
00:00:44,743 --> 00:00:58,877
So first of all, many thanks to Donatella who is translating for me.

4
00:00:59,819 --> 00:01:07,728
honeying my words with her angelic voice.

5
00:01:07,748 --> 00:01:13,335
Mamma mia, addolcendo le sue parole con la mia voce angelica.

6
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:17,361
Ecco.

7
00:01:17,381 --> 00:01:22,989
So I'm going to give a talk on the qualities of the Buddha, the nine qualities.

8
00:01:23,009 --> 00:01:25,691
So this is what we chant when we do puja.

9
00:01:26,465 --> 00:01:33,858
So this evening I will talk about the nine qualities of the Buddha, which we refer to when we intone the puja.

10
00:01:35,087 --> 00:02:00,656
So we chant that in the morning, eh?

11
00:02:01,462 --> 00:02:08,915
So the first quality is Arahant.

12
00:02:10,378 --> 00:02:23,741
And it means accomplished, somebody who is worthy of respect.

13
00:02:25,257 --> 00:02:31,967
Now, what the commentators do is they begin to separate the word to give it more meaning.

14
00:02:33,128 --> 00:02:39,318
Quello che fanno i commentatori è separano la parola dandogli un significato più vasto.

15
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:46,590
Ah, and the one that makes sense to me is the division between Ari and Hatta.

16
00:02:47,931 --> 00:02:52,800
La separazione che per me è più valida è quella tra Ari e Hatta.

17
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,024
It means he destroyed his enemies.

18
00:03:00,151 --> 00:03:04,419
Now the enemies, of course, are the defilements.

19
00:03:05,923 --> 00:03:16,223
Now the defilements are listed as ten.

20
00:03:16,776 --> 00:03:25,389
But actually in the scriptures it just means anything that is unwholesome within our personality.

21
00:03:26,491 --> 00:03:40,573
And such a person has no secret evil.

22
00:03:41,465 --> 00:03:47,570
Questa persona non ha alcuna male, alcuna cattiveria nascosta.

23
00:03:51,114 --> 00:04:07,590
And he can say with the Buddha, with all the enlightened people, that birth is destroyed and the holy life has been lived.

24
00:04:08,448 --> 00:04:19,805
che la nascita è distrutta e la vita sacra è conseguita.

25
00:04:20,767 --> 00:04:23,632
What had to be done has been done.

26
00:04:24,814 --> 00:04:28,120
Ciò che doveva essere compiuto è stato compiuto.

27
00:04:28,139 --> 00:04:31,805
There is no more rebirth for me.

28
00:04:32,562 --> 00:04:42,735
So whenever we say Arahant, that's what we mean.

29
00:04:44,357 --> 00:04:52,646
Now the second one is Sama Sambuddho, which means self-enlightened.

30
00:04:53,622 --> 00:04:59,314
La seconda è Sammasambuddha, che vuol dire autoilluminato.

31
00:05:00,076 --> 00:05:05,286
So this is the crucial role that the first person plays for us.

32
00:05:06,329 --> 00:05:13,824
E questo è il ruolo cruciale che la prima persona ha nei nostri confronti.

33
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:19,154
Somebody must have planted the first wheat.

34
00:05:20,536 --> 00:05:24,081
Qualcuno deve aver piantato the first wheat.

35
00:05:24,341 --> 00:05:25,822
What do you mean?

36
00:05:25,843 --> 00:05:26,343
Yeah, wheat.

37
00:05:28,365 --> 00:05:29,065
Yeah, grain.

38
00:05:29,086 --> 00:05:33,992
Sì, qualcuno ha piantato il primo stelo di grano.

39
00:05:35,754 --> 00:05:38,156
Somebody must have created the wheel.

40
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:43,744
Qualcuno deve avere creato la ruota.

41
00:05:44,213 --> 00:05:52,404
And we know that Edmund Hillary and Sherpa Tenzing climbed Everest.

42
00:05:53,627 --> 00:05:58,574
Sappiamo che queste due persone hanno conseguito l'Everest, hanno raggiunto l'Everest.

43
00:05:59,596 --> 00:06:03,802
So once they did it, everybody else can do it, even the dogs.

44
00:06:05,004 --> 00:06:11,233
Una volta che loro l'hanno fatto, vuol dire che anche tutti gli altri sono in grado di farlo, persino i cani.

45
00:06:11,617 --> 00:06:20,788
Ah, so in other words, the one who initiates, who begins something, has a special place within our praise.

46
00:06:22,028 --> 00:06:40,629
And so this means that the first person, the one who started all this, has a place, a special place in what we attribute to him, in the blessings we wish him.

47
00:06:41,538 --> 00:06:44,562
So he is the founder of our tradition.

48
00:06:46,125 --> 00:06:56,920
So without him there simply wouldn't be any Buddhism.

49
00:06:59,384 --> 00:07:03,951
Now the next quality is endowed with clear vision.

50
00:07:04,875 --> 00:07:12,543
quella successiva, la qualità successiva è dotato di chiara visione.

51
00:07:12,562 --> 00:07:15,125
Or we can say direct understanding.

52
00:07:16,326 --> 00:07:18,309
O di comprensione diretta.

53
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:22,994
And virtuous conduct.

54
00:07:24,095 --> 00:07:26,416
E anche di condotta virtuosa.

55
00:07:27,437 --> 00:07:32,723
So this means that he has understood the cause of our problems

56
00:07:33,648 --> 00:07:39,333
Questo vuol dire che gli ha compreso la causa dei nostri problemi.

57
00:07:40,194 --> 00:07:42,555
And of course of his own problems.

58
00:07:43,456 --> 00:07:47,139
Naturalmente partendo da quelli che erano i suoi propri problemi.

59
00:07:47,959 --> 00:07:51,702
And because of that his actions are always virtuous.

60
00:07:52,744 --> 00:07:57,067
E grazie a questo le sue azioni sono sempre virtuose.

61
00:07:57,949 --> 00:08:03,012
So remember that everything begins from this misunderstanding.

62
00:08:04,259 --> 00:08:13,812
It's a misunderstanding as to who we are.

63
00:08:14,894 --> 00:08:30,418
Presuming ourselves to be human beings, that's all, we seek happiness in the sensual world.

64
00:08:31,326 --> 00:08:49,230
Ah, and this creates what we call an attachment.

65
00:08:53,878 --> 00:08:58,683
Which means we are dependent on the sensual world to make us happy.

66
00:08:59,508 --> 00:09:05,716
Questo vuol dire che dipendiamo dal mondo sensoriale perché noi si possa essere felici.

67
00:09:06,738 --> 00:09:10,523
And this leads us to certain unfortunate qualities.

68
00:09:11,683 --> 00:09:16,370
E questo ci porta ad avere delle qualità sfortunate.

69
00:09:17,572 --> 00:09:20,996
Greed, aversion and fear.

70
00:09:21,977 --> 00:09:25,582
Avidità, avversione, paura.

71
00:09:25,681 --> 00:09:30,789
And all the rest?

72
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:33,234
All the rest of human misery.

73
00:09:34,195 --> 00:09:47,857
So, in other words, he is somebody who has understood the path and understands it to be a path of purification.

74
00:09:48,394 --> 00:10:00,596
Vuol dire che è stato colui che ha compreso il sentiero, il cammino da percorrere e che questo cammino è un sentiero, un cammino di purificazione.

75
00:10:00,616 --> 00:10:08,951
The next quality is translated as someone who has completed a journey.

76
00:10:10,044 --> 00:10:26,562
So this includes all the training that he went to with his two teachers.

77
00:10:27,563 --> 00:10:39,376
And his own discovery of the path.

78
00:10:40,133 --> 00:11:00,318
And don't forget that he also did some very severe mortification exercises.

79
00:11:00,956 --> 00:11:18,779
So in other words, by practicing in the wrong paths, he eventually found the right path.

80
00:11:24,748 --> 00:11:26,149
So this often happens to us.

81
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:29,934
First you make mistakes and then you find the right way to do something.

82
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:32,589
E questo è anche quello che accade a noi.

83
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:36,854
Prima facciamo degli errori e poi troviamo il modo giusto per fare le cose.

84
00:11:38,535 --> 00:11:41,659
Now the next one is a seer of the worlds.

85
00:11:43,081 --> 00:11:51,951
La qualità successiva è una persona che vede i mondi.

86
00:11:53,673 --> 00:12:00,140
Now, this does not refer specifically to seeing other realms of being.

87
00:12:00,863 --> 00:12:19,287
This is to do with the worlds that we create.

88
00:12:21,070 --> 00:12:27,477
These are the ones that we manufacture our little universes.

89
00:12:28,352 --> 00:12:35,822
Si tratta quindi di quei piccoli universi che noi stessi costruiamo, andiamo a costruire.

90
00:12:37,966 --> 00:12:42,873
So sometimes we're in the hell realm, when we're depressed and upset.

91
00:12:43,474 --> 00:12:51,465
A volte ci troviamo nella dimensione infernale, quando ci sentiamo molto infelici o depressi.

92
00:12:52,686 --> 00:12:57,533
Sometimes we were in the animal realm, when we used to get drunk, but we don't do that anymore.

93
00:12:58,373 --> 00:13:06,264
A volte ci trovavamo nel regno animale, per esempio, quando usavamo ubriacarci, ma ovviamente non lo facciamo più.

94
00:13:06,283 --> 00:13:11,770
And then there's the hungry ghost realm, when we are very greedy.

95
00:13:12,772 --> 00:13:20,883
Poi c'è la dimensione, il reame, diciamo, degli spiriti affamati, quando siamo pieni di avidità.

96
00:13:21,924 --> 00:13:28,092
And sometimes we're in the human realm, where we have some sort of intelligence, some sort of wisdom.

97
00:13:28,782 --> 00:13:50,283
Occasionally we get lost in anger and we become angry gods.

98
00:13:51,461 --> 00:13:59,615
And of course occasionally we are bathing in absolute wonderful joy and pleasure.

99
00:14:00,777 --> 00:14:18,785
So these are the worlds that we create within ourselves.

100
00:14:19,322 --> 00:14:23,509
So somehow we have to go beyond these worlds.

101
00:14:24,672 --> 00:14:28,879
In qualche modo dobbiamo riuscire ad andare oltre questi mondi.

102
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:33,647
And that's what we do whenever we practice vipassana.

103
00:14:34,427 --> 00:14:39,296
Ed è quello che facciamo ogni qualvolta pratichiamo la vipassana.

104
00:14:39,777 --> 00:14:44,605
Because when we practice vipassana we can see these worlds appearing in front of us.

105
00:14:44,938 --> 00:15:02,024
So this is, that was the knower of the worlds.

106
00:15:05,629 --> 00:15:14,000
The next is translates literally as a coachman driving an ox or a horse.

107
00:15:14,369 --> 00:15:26,553
E quello successivo si traduce come un guidatore che guida il carro trainato da un bue.

108
00:15:27,937 --> 00:15:35,533
It translates better as an incomparable trainer of trainees.

109
00:15:36,003 --> 00:15:45,393
Ah, si traduce meglio come un addestratore incomparabile di addestrati, di persone addestrate.

110
00:15:46,453 --> 00:15:51,278
And of course he has left us certain rules and regulations that we can follow.

111
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:59,606
Ovviamente ci ha lasciato delle regole, delle indicazioni che noi dobbiamo seguire.

112
00:16:00,207 --> 00:16:05,452
So on the negative side there are the five precepts, the eight precepts.

113
00:16:06,326 --> 00:16:13,979
And on the negative side there are the 5 and 8 precepts.

114
00:16:14,078 --> 00:16:30,225
And then of course for the monastic life, all the rules of the Vinaya.

115
00:16:30,947 --> 00:16:36,076
And on the positive side, he's given us the ten perfections.

116
00:16:37,879 --> 00:16:45,691
And the four Brahma Viharas, the four great illimitables.

117
00:16:50,378 --> 00:16:54,423
Love, compassion, joy and equanimity.

118
00:16:54,977 --> 00:17:06,079
La gentilezza amorevole, la compassione, la gioia compartecipe e la equanimità.

119
00:17:08,545 --> 00:17:14,656
The next one is, he is a teacher of gods and men.

120
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:19,265
Gods and human beings.

121
00:17:19,726 --> 00:17:26,074
Quello successivo è un insegnante di dei e esseri umani.

122
00:17:26,994 --> 00:17:27,855
Ah, esseri umani.

123
00:17:28,876 --> 00:17:33,402
So this, of course, refers to the Dharma, all the teachings of the Dharma.

124
00:17:34,282 --> 00:17:37,666
Questo ovviamente si riferisce a tutti gli insegnamenti del Dharma.

125
00:17:38,989 --> 00:17:42,432
And, of course, the practice of Vipassana.

126
00:17:43,038 --> 00:17:48,987
Of all the absorption techniques.

127
00:17:50,229 --> 00:18:05,551
And, of course, how to live the spiritual life in ordinary daily life.

128
00:18:07,522 --> 00:18:12,490
And number eight is buddho which is the one who knows.

129
00:18:13,491 --> 00:18:17,458
L'ottavo è buddho, cioè colui che conosce.

130
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:27,752
So this is simply saying that he knows how we create the world of samsara, the world of ongoing.

131
00:18:28,814 --> 00:18:36,045
Questo vuol dire semplicemente colui che conosce il modo in cui noi costruiamo il mondo del samsara.

132
00:18:37,865 --> 00:18:38,625
And the escape.

133
00:18:42,931 --> 00:18:50,859
So remember he said he only taught two things.

134
00:18:51,861 --> 00:18:56,987
Dukkha and the end of Dukkha.

135
00:18:57,528 --> 00:19:06,858
And Dukkha is all the miseries that you can think of.

136
00:19:07,884 --> 00:19:13,893
And then the final quality is Bhagavā, which means exalted, sublime.

137
00:19:13,952 --> 00:19:29,633
Yes, it's an honorific, like we say of the Dalai Lama, his holiness.

138
00:19:30,554 --> 00:19:37,403
Yes, it's an honorific term, like when we refer to the Dalai Lama as his holiness.

139
00:19:38,615 --> 00:19:46,928
So those nine qualities he has accomplished and has destroyed all his defilements.

140
00:19:47,729 --> 00:19:56,864
Quindi queste nove qualità ha raggiunto e distrutto, è arrivato alla fine della strada, ha distrutto tutti gli inquinanti.

141
00:19:58,105 --> 00:19:59,689
He was self-awakened.

142
00:20:00,630 --> 00:20:03,795
Autoilluminato, autorisvegliato.

143
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:12,791
He has a clear understanding of our situation and because of that virtuous conduct.

144
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:21,964
He has completed the journey and he did it skillfully.

145
00:20:22,005 --> 00:20:33,039
He knows all the worlds that we can create and how to get out of them.

146
00:20:33,829 --> 00:20:40,357
conosce tutti i mondi che siamo in grado di creare in noi stessi e anche i modi per poterne uscire.

147
00:20:41,239 --> 00:20:43,883
He's a wonderful trainer, a coach.

148
00:20:45,023 --> 00:20:50,030
È un addestratore, un istruttore straordinario.

149
00:20:50,530 --> 00:20:51,972
Yeah, life coach.

150
00:20:53,054 --> 00:20:54,695
Un istruttore di vita.

151
00:20:55,798 --> 00:20:57,359
And he's also a great teacher.

152
00:20:57,400 --> 00:21:00,663
Ed è anche un grande insegnante.

153
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:08,367
He has penetrated the human condition, he is the Buddha.

154
00:21:08,528 --> 00:21:24,406
And therefore we consider him to be exalted, sublime and blessed.

155
00:21:24,606 --> 00:21:43,025
So I hope my words have been of some assistance.

156
00:21:44,705 --> 00:21:51,593
Oh, sorry.

157
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:55,305
That's this silly Google assistant.

158
00:21:56,686 --> 00:22:08,607
A very great annoyance.

159
00:22:10,069 --> 00:22:15,960
So I hope my words have been of some assistance.

160
00:22:16,665 --> 00:22:21,393
Quindi spero che le mie parole vi siano state di aiuto, di ispirazione.

161
00:22:21,913 --> 00:22:24,477
That I have not caused confusion.

162
00:22:25,338 --> 00:22:29,304
Spero di non avere contribuito a confusione invece.

163
00:22:30,205 --> 00:22:33,450
And that by your devotion to the past you will be liberated.

164
00:22:33,470 --> 00:22:40,641
E che grazie alla vostra devozione nei confronti del cammino voi possiate essere liberati.

165
00:22:41,682 --> 00:22:44,226
Sooner rather than later.

166
00:22:44,729 --> 00:22:49,186
prima piuttosto che più tardi, più in avanti nel tempo.

